silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_03_typed_verb_discipline_sections_01_typed_verb_rule_concrete_anchor_1_v#hasasbodymassarrow silm:hasLongDescription "The HasAsBodyMassArrow is the typed-verb candidate 'has as body mass'. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'v', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
